# Two determinism pins live under this directory, and both are re-asserted on the cross-platform
# job's live legs — Linux x64 and Android ARM64. (The iOS ARM64 leg is authored and gated off with
# iOS itself, `16` D34.)
#
#   CombatLogReferenceVectors.json         — 05 §7's LogHash byte encoding
#   Determinism/BattleLogHashBaseline.json — 14 §8.2's 10 000 (seed, build, enemy) triples
#
# ⚠️ The first of these was NOT covered by a rule until M5-12 added this file: it inherited the
# repository root's `* text=auto`, which normalises to LF in the index but hands the working tree
# whatever the platform prefers. That was harmless while nothing off-host read it. Pinning eol=lf
# makes it byte-identical on every leg, and makes a one-row addition diff as one row rather than as a
# whole-file rewrite because someone's core.autocrlf disagreed. Same rule as Rng/, Model/Snapshots/,
# Rules/Effects/Determinism/ and game-data/.
*.json text eol=lf
